qwen27b-jev


Jev-style semantic decisions on Qwen3.8-27B.


Most agent decisions are small: route this, retry that, does the
evidence support X. A chat model can answer them, but it spends
time generating text that software immediately parses back into
an if statement.

This reads typed option probabilities directly from the model.
One forward pass, softmax over the logits of the answer letters
A..P at the first generation position. No token is sampled, no
JSON is parsed, no grammar is enforced. A long state can be
prefilled once and branched across many questions.


    from jev import Jev

    llm = Jev()
    llm.decide(state, question, {"yes": "It succeeded.", "no": "It did not."})
    llm.decide_many(state, [(question, options), ...])

    $ ./run.sh uv run example.py


Interface and prompt follow OpenJev, which did this with a 4B
model. This swaps in the 27B. See PLAN.md.


References:

- OpenJev: https://github.com/TheoLeeCJ/openjev
- Jev: https://typesafe.ai
- Qwen3.8-27B: https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B
